# Every text file under App and Preparation is checked out with plain line
# endings on every system, Windows included.
#
# Without this, the hosted Windows runner checks each text file out with
# Windows line endings, and the application's tests read source files, page
# files, the mockup and the plans as text. A test that looks for a line holding
# only a closing brace found it on the Mac and on Linux and not on Windows, and
# eight tests went red on run 34759561814 for that reason alone. The account is
# `Audits/Build/Step 10a/The red run of 2026-09-13 — what it was.md`.
#
# The hosted workflows are held to the same, because a test reads the workflow
# as text too. Run 34767216812 went red on Windows on exactly that one test
# after the first two lines were in place.
#
# Apart from COPYING below, it is limited to those three folders on purpose.
# Audits keeps raw output captured on a Windows machine, with that machine's
# own line endings, and those bytes are evidence and are left as written.
#
# A test in `App/Desktop app and delivery/src/the_selected_shell.rs` asks git
# whether this still holds for every file, and fails if it does not.
/App/** text=auto eol=lf
/Preparation/** text=auto eol=lf
/.github/** text=auto eol=lf

# About embeds this licence unchanged. Keep its bytes the same in Windows
# builds, the drawing's offline reader and the public repository.
/COPYING text eol=lf
